    "text": "I had always assumed that juggling was a talent you were born with, but last summer I decided to prove myself wrong. My plan was simple: ten minutes of practice every day, no matter [[1]] tired I felt. For the first week I dropped the balls so often [[2]] my cat began to hide under the sofa. I almost gave up, but a friend who [[3]] been learning for a year told me to stick [[4]] my routine.\n\nShe also taught me a useful trick: instead of watching the balls, look at a point just above your head. Slowly, the balls began to move [[5]] a smooth circle. After three weeks I could keep three balls in the air for [[6]] least a minute, and I felt as proud as if I had won a prize. Now, whenever I feel stressed, I pick up the balls and juggle until the worry begins to let [[7]]. It is [[8]] only a good hobby, but also a great way to calm the mind.",
